<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/flooded-dock.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/flooded-dock-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/flooded-dock.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="681" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/service-locations/">Locations</a></li><li aria-current="page">Salisbury</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Eastern Shore · Wicomico County</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser for Salisbury and Lower Shore Claims</h1><p class="lede">Salisbury is the hub of the lower Eastern Shore, where hurricane deductibles, wind-driven rain and low-lying land shape many claims. Our work as insurance appraiser in Salisbury, MD focuses on getting the wind portion of those losses paid fairly.</p><div class="btns"><a class="btn brass" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn ghost-l" href="/start-a-claim-review/">Request a free review</a></div><dl class="ph-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Wicomico County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Eastern Shore</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose"><div class="localcard"><div><h2 class="lc-h">Local claim risks</h2><ul class="chips"><li>Hurricane and tropical storm wind</li><li>Nor’easters</li><li>Wind-driven rain</li><li>Tidal flooding</li><li>Tree strikes</li></ul></div><div><h2 class="lc-h">Storms on record</h2><ul class="dots"><li>Hurricane Isabel, 2003</li><li>Superstorm Sandy, 2012</li><li>Ash Wednesday nor’easter, 1962</li></ul></div><div class="full"><h2 class="lc-h">Housing mix</h2><p>Older homes in Salisbury’s historic neighborhoods such as Newtown, mid-century and newer single-family homes, student rentals near Salisbury University, and farm properties across Wicomico County.</p><p class="hoods"><b>Neighborhoods &amp; nearby:</b> Downtown Salisbury, Newtown, Fruitland, Delmar, Hebron, Pittsville, Princess Anne</p></div></div><h2>The lower Shore’s claim landscape</h2>
<p>Salisbury is the county seat of Wicomico County and the largest city on Maryland’s Eastern Shore, set on the Wicomico River where US 13 and US 50 meet. Much of the surrounding land is flat and low, and the Chesapeake Bay and Atlantic coast are both within reach of major storms. An insurance appraiser in Salisbury, MD spends a lot of time on wind claims and on questions about hurricane deductibles.</p>
<h2>Hurricane deductibles on the Eastern Shore</h2>
<p>Percentage hurricane, named-storm and windstorm deductibles are common on the Eastern Shore. A 2% or 5% deductible on the dwelling limit can be a large sum, and the trigger definitions vary by insurer. Before accepting a payment, confirm which deductible was applied and whether the event actually met the trigger. Our <a href="/knowledge-base/bay-hurricane-deductibles/">Bay hurricane deductibles guide</a> explains how these usually work.</p>
<h2>Storm history and how it shows up in claims</h2>
<p>Hurricane Isabel in 2003 brought surge and wind across the Bay side of the Shore, and Superstorm Sandy in 2012 caused coastal flooding in communities such as Crisfield in neighboring Somerset County. The 1962 Ash Wednesday nor’easter remains a benchmark coastal storm for the region. In claims, these storms typically produce:</p>
<ul>
<li>Roof and siding damage from sustained wind, often disputed as wear on older materials</li>
<li>Interior water from wind-driven rain, sometimes reclassified as flood</li>
<li>Tree damage to roofs, fences and outbuildings</li>
<li>Disagreement over whether a hurricane or ordinary deductible applies</li>
</ul>
<p>Rising water and storm surge are generally excluded from homeowners policies and need separate flood insurance, so documenting wind damage clearly is important.</p>
<h2>Communities we serve around Salisbury</h2>
<p>We inspect in downtown Salisbury and the historic Newtown neighborhood, as well as Fruitland, Delmar, Hebron, Pittsville and Princess Anne. Rental properties near Salisbury University and farm buildings across the county raise their own questions about landlord policies and other structures coverage.</p>
<p>Salisbury itself sits inland on the Wicomico River, so many local claims are wind and tree losses rather than surge. Older homes in Newtown and around downtown often have plaster, wood siding and slate or older shingles that are expensive to match. Newer homes on the edges of town have vinyl siding and architectural shingles, which wind can lift and crease without obvious tearing. Both types need a careful look before the estimate is accepted.</p>
<h2>Practical steps for Wicomico County owners</h2>
<p>Photograph exterior wind damage from every side, and separately document any water line inside. Keep a record of the storm’s date and any watches or warnings issued, since some deductibles depend on them. If you have both flood and homeowners coverage, keep both claims moving and share what you’re claiming under each.</p>
<p>Maryland Insurance Appraiser can review the wind portion of your claim and represent you through appraisal if the amount is disputed. Questions about coverage or deductible triggers can go to a Maryland attorney.</p><h2>Services for Salisbury property owners</h2><p>Every service is available in Salisbury and the rest of Wicomico County, including:</p><ul class="cols2"><li><a href="/property-claim-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/home-insurance-appraisal/">Home Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/roof-hail-damage-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/windstorm-tornado-appraisal/">Windstorm &amp; Tornado Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/hurricane-noreaster-appraisal/">Hurricane &amp; Nor’easter Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/water-damage-appraisal/">Water Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/fire-smoke-damage-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Salisbury claim questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How do I know if my hurricane deductible applies in Salisbury?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Look at your declarations page and the deductible endorsement. Some policies trigger the hurricane deductible only when a named storm or hurricane watch or warning is issued, while others use broader windstorm language. Ask your carrier to explain in writing which trigger it relied on.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is wind-driven rain covered on the Eastern Shore?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Interior water damage is often covered when wind first damages the roof, walls or windows and rain then enters through that opening. Rain that enters without any wind damage, or rising water, is usually treated differently. Check your policy’s wording.</p></div></details></div><h2>Nearby service areas</h2><div class="rel"><a href="/service-locations/ocean-city/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Ocean City</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/service-locations/annapolis/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Annapolis</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/service-locations/bowie/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Bowie</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article><aside class="side"><div class="side-in"><div class="box box-call"><h2 class="box-h">Talk to an appraiser</h2><p>A free first conversation about yo